summary:
  Play after a pause never goes on in the player: the kept file is always
  opened again.

history:
  A file the player still holds, paused, plays on from its needle at once.
  Opening it again is for the roads where that cannot work: an episode that
  streams, whose server drops a connection nobody reads from, and a pause
  something else took out of the player. Taking that road for every file
  costs a reload and the start's fade on each Play, and the place is only
  good to the second.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
      var lifts = shifted === true || (pausedFile === true && inPlace === true);

replace:
      var lifts = shifted === true;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_a_file_the_player_still_holds_simply_plays_on
  and tests/qml/tst_transportroads.qml::test_play_after_the_pause_goes_on_in_place.
  Line-neutral.
